# Harness OUTPUTS, not harness code. The scripts are tracked so anyone can run
# them; their results are per-run artifacts and must never be committed.
#
# (These were being written straight into this tracked folder, against the
# dev-mode plan's own rule that outputs belong in DEBUG/output/get_earth/.
# Ignoring them here is the narrower fix -- it keeps the driver scripts
# self-contained instead of splitting each run across two trees.)
l3_*_result.json
l3_*_capture.png
*.part
__pycache__/

# Re-include pytest files. The REPO-ROOT .gitignore line 218 is a bare
# `test_*.py`, which silently excludes every pytest-convention test file
# anywhere in the tree -- these two suites staged as nothing at all until
# `git check-ignore -v` named the rule. A nested negation is the scoped fix; it
# does not touch shared repo-wide config.
#
# The root rule is worth revisiting on its own (it makes a conventional test
# suite unaddable anywhere in this repo), but that is a separate, deliberate
# change -- not a signoff-time edit.
!test_*.py
